"Encode a quantity as a strict-JSON-compatible dictionary (see the module "
"docstring)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:1 of
msgid "Check that ``value`` is a quantity convertible to ``unit`` and return it."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:3 of
msgid ""
"The quantity is returned unchanged (same object, same unit), so the "
"user's unit is preserved. Plain numbers are only accepted when ``unit`` "
"is dimensionless; they are then wrapped in a dimensionless quantity."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:7 of
msgid "The value to check."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:8 of
msgid "Expected unit, or any unit with the same physical dimension."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:9 of
msgid "Name of the checked value, used in error messages."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:10 of
msgid ""
"Optional astropy equivalencies, e.g. ``u.spectral()`` to accept a "
"frequency for a wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/index.md
msgid "Returns"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:12 of
msgid "The validated quantity."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:15 of
msgid ""
"If ``value`` is not a quantity (or not numeric) while a dimensional unit "
"is expected."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.require_unit:16 of
msgid "If the unit of ``value`` cannot be converted to ``unit``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.si_unit:1 of
msgid "Return the unscaled SI unit with the same dimension as ``unit``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.si_unit:3 of
msgid ""
"For example ``nm`` gives ``m``, ``deg`` gives ``rad``, ``Jy`` gives ``kg "
"/ s2`` and ``%`` gives the dimensionless unit. Irreducible non-SI units "
"(such as ``ph``) are kept."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.to_si:1 of
msgid "Return the numerical value of ``quantity`` in unscaled SI units."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.to_si:3 of
msgid "The quantity to convert."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.to_si:4 of
msgid ""
"Optional target dimension; defaults to the dimension of ``quantity``. Use"
" it with ``equivalencies`` to convert across dimensions (e.g. frequency "
"to wavelength)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.to_si:6 of
msgid "Optional astropy equivalencies."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.units.to_si:8 of
msgid "A Python scalar for scalar quantities, an array otherwise."
msgstr ""

