#: lumos.backend.fft:1 of
msgid "Two-dimensional FFTs on any backend."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft:3 of
msgid ""
"Every function works on the backend of its input array: JAX arrays are "
"transformed by JAX, CuPy arrays on the GPU, and NumPy arrays by "
":mod:`scipy.fft`, which keeps single precision and uses "
"``lumos.config.fft_workers`` CPU threads."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft:7 of
msgid ""
"The *centred* transforms :func:`fft2c` and :func:`ifft2c` assume that the"
" origin of both the input and the output grids is the pixel of index ``N "
"// 2`` along each axis (convention of LUMOS, §9 of the specs). They are "
"the natural transforms for optics, where fields are centred on the "
"optical axis."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft.fft2:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the discrete Fourier transform of ``array`` over ``axes`` (origin "
"at index 0)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft.fft2c:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the centred Fourier transform of ``array`` (origins of both grids "
"at index ``N // 2``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft.fftfreq:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the sample frequencies of an ``n``-point FFT with sample spacing "
"``d``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft.fftfreq:3 of
msgid ""
"The array is created with ``backend`` (the current backend by default), "
"in FFT order (zero first)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft.fftshift:1 of
msgid ""
"Move the zero-frequency sample from index 0 to index ``N // 2`` along "
"``axes``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft.ifft2:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the inverse discrete Fourier transform of ``array`` over ``axes`` "
"(origin at index 0)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft.ifft2c:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the centred inverse Fourier transform of ``array`` (inverse of "
":func:`fft2c`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.fft.ifftshift:1 of
msgid ""
"Inverse of :func:`fftshift`: move the sample at index ``N // 2`` to index"
" 0 along ``axes``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.hardware:1 of
msgid "Hardware detection and automatic backend selection (REQ-HPC-2, ADR-0004)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.hardware:3 of
msgid ""
":func:`hardware_report` describes the machine LUMOS runs on: operating "
"system, CPU, memory, GPUs seen by the installed backends and versions of "
"the main libraries. The report is stored in archive metadata (REQ-RES-2) "
"and drives :func:`select_backend`, used when ``lumos.config.backend`` is "
"``\"auto\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.hardware.GPUInfo:1 of
msgid "A GPU (or other accelerator) seen by a backend."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.hardware.HardwareReport:1 of
msgid "Description of the machine and software environment."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.hardware.HardwareReport.to_dict:1 of
msgid "Return the report as plain data (YAML and JSON serialisable)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.hardware.HardwareReport.summary:1 of
msgid "Return a short human-readable description."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.hardware.select_backend:1 of
msgid ""
"Choose the backend to use on the machine described by ``report`` (policy "
"of ADR-0004)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.hardware.select_backend:3 of
msgid ""
"A GPU backend is chosen when it sees a GPU, JAX first, then CuPy, then "
"PyTorch; otherwise NumPy, the CPU reference."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory:1 of
msgid ""
"Numerical precision, memory estimates and chunked computation (REQ-HPC-4,"
" REQ-HPC-5)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory:3 of
msgid ""
"Large computations (a wavecube of hundreds of wavelengths, thousands of "
"incoherent modes...) may not fit in memory at once. Most of them are "
"independent along one axis, so :func:`map_chunked` cuts the input along "
"that axis into chunks that fit a memory budget, applies the computation "
"to each chunk and concatenates the results, which are identical to those "
"of a single computation."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.available_memory:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the memory in bytes currently available to ``backend`` (the "
"current backend by default)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.available_memory:3 of
msgid ""
"CPU backends report the available RAM; GPU backends report the free "
"memory of their first device."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.chunk_slices:1 of
msgid ""
"Split ``range(n)`` into consecutive slices of at most ``budget_bytes // "
"item_bytes`` items."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.chunk_slices:3 of
msgid ""
"Every chunk holds at least one item, even when a single item exceeds the "
"budget."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.dtypes:1 of
msgid "Return the ``(real, complex)`` dtypes of ``backend`` for ``precision``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.dtypes:3 of
msgid ""
"``\"double\"`` (float64 / complex128) or ``\"single\"`` (float32 / "
"complex64); defaults to ``lumos.config.precision``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.dtypes:5 of
msgid "Backend name; defaults to the current backend."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.estimate_bytes:1 of
msgid "Return the size in bytes of an array of ``shape`` and ``dtype``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.map_chunked:1 of
msgid ""
"Apply ``function`` to chunks of ``array`` along ``axis`` and concatenate "
"the results."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.map_chunked:3 of
msgid ""
"``function`` must treat the elements along ``axis`` independently and "
"keep their number (for example a 2-D FFT applied to every wavelength of a"
" cube). The result equals ``function(array)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.map_chunked:6 of
msgid "Computation to apply; it receives and returns arrays of the same backend."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.map_chunked:7 of
msgid "Input array."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.map_chunked:8 of
msgid "Axis along which the input is cut."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.backend.memory.map_chunked:9 of
msgid ""
"Maximum size of the input of one chunk; defaults to a quarter of the "
"memory available to the backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../api/index.md:39
msgid "Core"
msgstr "Cœur"

#: lumos.core.param:1 of
msgid ""
"Declarative fields of LUMOS objects: physical parameters, settings and "
"state (REQ-EL-1 to REQ-EL-3)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:3 of
msgid ""
"A class derived from :class:`ParamHost` declares its fields as class "
"attributes::"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:10 of
msgid "Three kinds of fields exist:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:12 of
msgid ""
":class:`Param`: a physical quantity (always an "
":class:`astropy.units.Quantity`) describing the configuration of an "
"object, such as a focal length;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:14 of
msgid ""
":class:`State`: a physical quantity changed by the actions of an "
"equipment, such as a stage position;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:15 of
msgid ""
":class:`Setting`: a non-physical value (integer, string, boolean, "
"choice), such as a method name."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:17 of
msgid "For every physical field the host keeps two values:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:19 of
msgid ""
"the **user value**, exactly as given (same number, same unit), returned "
"when the attribute is read, so that ``550 nm`` is never displayed as "
"``550.0000000001 nm``;"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:21 of
msgid ""
"the **SI value**, a float, complex or read-only array in unscaled SI "
"units, returned by :meth:`ParamHost.si` for the numerical kernels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param:24 of
msgid ""
"Arrays are copied on assignment and stored read-only, so they cannot be "
"modified behind the host's back: every change goes through an assignment,"
" which calls :meth:`ParamHost._on_field_changed` (used to invalidate "
"cached results)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:1 of
msgid "A physical parameter of a LUMOS object."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:3 of
msgid ""
"Unit (or any unit of the same dimension) of the parameter; ``None`` for a"
" dimensionless parameter."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:4 of
msgid "Default value. It is validated when the parameter is declared."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:5 of
msgid ""
"``(low, high)`` limits, each a quantity or ``None``. They apply to every "
"element of an array."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:6 of
msgid "Whether ``low`` and ``high`` are allowed values."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:7 of
msgid ""
"Required shape: ``()`` for a scalar (default), a tuple for a fixed shape,"
" ``None`` for any shape."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:8 of
msgid "``\"real\"`` (default) or ``\"complex\"``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:9 of
msgid ""
"Description of the parameter (shown in the documentation, the web "
"interface and the MCP server)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:10 of
msgid ""
"Whether the parameter is free (fitted by calibration or inference) by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:11 of
msgid "Default prior distribution of the parameter when it is free."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:12 of
msgid "Whether gradients with respect to this parameter are meaningful."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param:13 of
msgid ""
"Astropy equivalencies accepted for this parameter, e.g. ``u.spectral()`` "
"for a wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param.check_prior:1 of
msgid "Check that ``prior`` describes values of this parameter's dimension."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Param.validate:1 of
msgid "Check ``value`` and return ``(user_value, si_value)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.ParamHost:1 of
msgid ""
"Base class of objects declaring :class:`Param`, :class:`State` and "
":class:`Setting` fields."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.ParamHost:3 of
msgid ""
"Keyword arguments of the constructor set the fields; fields without a "
"default are required."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.ParamHost.declared:1 of
msgid "Return the declared fields, in definition order (inherited fields first)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.ParamHost.si:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the value of field ``name`` in unscaled SI units (settings are "
"returned as is)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.ParamHost.is_free:1 of
msgid "Whether parameter ``name`` is free (fitted by calibration or inference)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.ParamHost.prior:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the prior of parameter ``name`` (``None`` if fixed or without "
"prior)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.ParamHost.set_free:1 of
msgid ""
"Mark parameter ``name`` as free (with an optional prior) or fixed, for "
"this object only."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Setting:1 of
msgid ""
"A non-physical setting: an integer, a float without unit, a string or a "
"boolean."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Setting:3 of
msgid ""
"Expected Python type. Booleans are not accepted for ``int`` or ``float`` "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Setting:4 of
msgid "Default value, validated when the setting is declared."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Setting:5 of
msgid "Optional collection of allowed values."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Setting:6 of
msgid "Description of the setting."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.param.Setting.validate:1 of
msgid "Check ``value`` and return it twice (settings have no SI form)."
