#: lumos.fields.smatrix:1 of
msgid "Scattering matrices of guided-wave components (REQ-SIG-7)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A component with :math:`n_\\mathrm{in}` input and :math:`n_\\mathrm{out}`"
" output channels maps the modal amplitudes :math:`a` to :math:`S a`, with"
" :math:`S` of shape ``(n_out, n_in)`` or, for a wavelength-dependent "
"component, ``(nλ, n_out, n_in)``. Lossless reciprocal components have "
"unitary matrices, :math:`S^\\dagger S = 1` (Pozar, *Microwave "
"Engineering*, §4.3), and conserve the power."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix:8 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Phases follow the :math:`e^{-i\\omega t}` convention of §9 of the "
"specifications: :math:`e^{+i\\phi}` is a delay."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.coupler:1 of
msgid ""
"Symmetric lossless directional coupler with power coupling ratio "
"``ratio`` (``κ²``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.coupler:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"S = \\begin{pmatrix} t & i\\kappa \\\\ i\\kappa & t \\end{pmatrix}, "
"\\qquad t = \\sqrt{1 - \\kappa^2}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.coupler:5 of
msgid ""
"(Okamoto, *Fundamentals of Optical Waveguides*, §4.4). ``ratio = 0.5`` is"
" the 50/50 coupler."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.is_unitary:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether a square matrix (or every matrix of a stack) satisfies ``S^† S = "
"1`` within ``atol``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.smatrix.phase_shifter:1 of
msgid "Diagonal matrix applying the phase ``phases[j]`` to channel ``j``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:1 of
msgid "Sampling of a spectral band for polychromatic computations (REQ-SIG-4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:3 of
msgid ""
"A polychromatic quantity is integrated over a band with a quadrature "
"rule: wavelengths :math:`\\lambda_k` and weights :math:`w_k` such that"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:6 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\frac{1}{\\Delta\\lambda}\\int_{\\lambda_0 - "
"\\Delta\\lambda/2}^{\\lambda_0 + \\Delta\\lambda/2}\n"
"f(\\lambda)\\,d\\lambda \\approx \\sum_k w_k f(\\lambda_k), \\qquad "
"\\sum_k w_k = 1 .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:9 of
msgid ""
"``\"midpoint\"``: ``n`` equal panels sampled at their centres, equal "
"weights ``1/n``; exact for linear spectra, robust for any spectrum."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral:11 of
msgid ""
"``\"gauss\"``: Gauss-Legendre nodes and weights; exact for polynomials of"
" degree ``2n - 1``, the most accurate choice for smooth spectra."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:1 of
msgid "Return wavelengths and normalised weights sampling a band."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:3 of
msgid "Central wavelength of the band."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:4 of
msgid "Full width of the band; the band must stay at positive wavelengths."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:5 of
msgid "Number of samples."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:6 of
msgid "``\"midpoint\"`` or ``\"gauss\"`` (Gauss-Legendre)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:8 of
msgid ""
"* **wavelengths** (*astropy.units.Quantity*) -- ``n`` wavelengths in the "
"unit of ``center``. * **weights** (*numpy.ndarray*) -- ``n`` weights "
"summing to 1 (band average)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:8 of
msgid ""
"**wavelengths** (*astropy.units.Quantity*) -- ``n`` wavelengths in the "
"unit of ``center``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.spectral.spectral_samples:9 of
msgid ""
"**weights** (*numpy.ndarray*) -- ``n`` weights summing to 1 (band "
"average)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:1 of
msgid ""
"Polarisation: Jones vectors, Jones matrices and Stokes parameters (REQ-"
"SIG-3)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:3 of
msgid ""
"A polarised :class:`~lumos.fields.Wavefront` holds the Jones components "
":math:`(E_x, E_y)` in the laboratory basis along the first axis of its "
"field, of shape ``(2, ny, nx)``. Polarising elements multiply it by a "
":math:`2 \\times 2` Jones matrix, uniform (shape ``(2, 2)``) or varying "
"across the grid (shape ``(2, 2, ny, nx)``), with :func:`apply`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:9 of
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:10 of
msgid "Angles are measured from +x towards +y."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:11 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"With the time dependence :math:`e^{-i\\omega t}` of §9 of the "
"specifications, a phase factor :math:`e^{+i\\phi}` is a delay. A retarder"
" of retardance :math:`\\Gamma` with its fast axis along x is "
":math:`\\mathrm{diag}(1, e^{i\\Gamma})`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:14 of
msgid "Stokes parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:16 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"S_0 = |E_x|^2 + |E_y|^2,\\quad S_1 = |E_x|^2 - |E_y|^2,\\quad\n"
"S_2 = 2\\,\\mathrm{Re}(E_x^* E_y),\\quad S_3 = 2\\,\\mathrm{Im}(E_x^* "
"E_y).\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones:19 of
msgid ""
"The right circular state :math:`R = (1, i)/\\sqrt 2` turns clockwise for "
"an observer facing the source and has :math:`S_3 = +S_0` (Born & Wolf, "
"*Principles of Optics*, §1.4.2)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.apply:1 of
msgid ""
"Apply a Jones matrix to a polarised wavefront, wavecube (every channel) "
"or bundle (every mode)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.apply:3 of
msgid ""
"Shape ``(2, 2)`` (uniform) or ``(2, 2, ny, nx)`` (varying across the "
"grid), any backend."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.apply:4 of
msgid ""
"Polarised :class:`~lumos.fields.Wavefront` (field ``(2, ny, nx)``) or "
":class:`~lumos.fields.Wavecube` (field ``(nλ, 2, ny, nx)``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.degree_of_polarization:1 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Return :math:`\\sqrt{S_1^2 + S_2^2 + S_3^2} / S_0` for Stokes parameters "
"along the first axis."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.half_wave_plate:1 of
msgid "Half-wave plate (retardance π) with its fast axis at ``angle``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.linear:1 of
msgid "Return the Jones vector of a linear polarisation at ``angle`` from x."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.polarizer:1 of
msgid ""
"Ideal linear polariser transmitting the polarisation at ``angle`` (a "
"projector)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.quarter_wave_plate:1 of
msgid "Quarter-wave plate (retardance π/2) with its fast axis at ``angle``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.retarder:1 of
msgid ""
"Linear retarder of retardance :math:`\\Gamma` with its fast axis at "
"``angle``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.retarder:3 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid "The slow axis is delayed by :math:`e^{i\\Gamma}`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.rotator:1 of
msgid ""
"Polarisation rotator turning every linear polarisation by ``angle`` (e.g."
" a Faraday rotator)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.stokes:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the Stokes parameters ``(S0, S1, S2, S3)``, shape ``(4, ny, nx)`` "
"or ``(nλ, 4, ny, nx)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.stokes:3 of
msgid ""
"They are in the intensity unit of the signal. For an "
":class:`~lumos.fields.IncoherentBundle`, the Stokes parameters of the "
"modes add with the mode weights (incoherent superposition, Born & Wolf "
"§10.8.3), which describes partially polarised and natural light."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.vector:1 of
msgid "Return the normalised Jones vector of a basis state."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.jones.vector:3 of
msgid ""
"``\"H\"`` (horizontal, x), ``\"V\"`` (vertical, y), ``\"D\"`` (diagonal, "
"+45°), ``\"A\"`` (anti-diagonal, -45°), ``\"R\"`` (right circular) or "
"``\"L\"`` (left circular)."
msgstr ""

