#: lumos.core.graph:1 of
msgid ""
"Directed acyclic graph of elements connected port to port, with pull "
"execution (REQ-CTX-1/2/4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`Graph` holds elements under unique identifiers and the "
"connections between their ports. A connection goes from an output port to"
" an input port whose signal type is the same or a base class (REQ-"
"SIG-11). The graph is acyclic: physical loops (adaptive optics, servo "
"loops, iterative calibration) are iterations in time driven by the "
"context, not cycles of signals."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph:8 of
msgid ""
"Execution is *pull*: :meth:`Graph.run` computes only the elements needed "
"by the requested outputs, in topological order. The outputs of every "
"element are cached; changing a parameter or a state of an element, or a "
"connection, invalidates the cache of that element and of everything "
"downstream."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.core.graph.Connection:1 of
